{#
  Compatibility route for the original Speedlify's API.

  A `<speedlify-score>` component with no `hash` attribute fetches this to turn a
  URL into one, then requests /api/<hash>.json. Without it that path 404s and the
  component fails outright.

  Deliberately minimal: the component reads `.hash` and nothing else, so nothing
  else is emitted. The original also carries requestedUrl, url, categories and
  vertical here — absent, because no consumer fails without them.

  Only the URLs the original instance published, from the frozen snapshot in
  config/legacy-api-urls.json — not our own site list. An embed can only exist
  for a URL that instance served, so those are the only keys worth having;
  adding our 1,600 would be 1,600 entries nothing looks up.

  Keyed by the URL as a bare string. The lookup is `json[url]` with no
  normalization at all, so the key has to be spelled the way the original spelled
  it — `https://example.com/about/`, where we store the slash stripped.

  Built from the same `compatRoutes` list as the per-hash files, so the index
  cannot name a hash that was never written.
-#}
{
{%- for route in sites.compatRoutes %}
  {{ route.url | dump | safe }}: { "hash": {{ route.hash | dump | safe }} }{{ "," if not loop.last }}
{%- endfor %}
}
